---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import '../../../styles/detail.css';

const title = 'Steel Structure Warehouse | Prefabricated Warehouse Building | ZhongSai';
const description = 'ZhongSai Steel Structure provides steel structure warehouse and logistics building solutions, covering design detailing, fabrication, component supply, packing and export delivery, with support for racking layout, clear height planning, loading access and enclosure system configuration.';
const lang = 'en';
const canonical = 'https://zhongsai-steelstructure.com/en/steel-warehouse/';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="detail-hero">
    <div class="detail-hero-bg" style="background-image: url('/images/products/app-warehouse-logistics-hero.jpg');"></div>
    <div class="detail-hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="detail-hero-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Steel Warehouse · Logistics Building</span>
      <h1>Steel Structure Warehouse & Logistics Building</h1>
      <p class="lead">ZhongSai Steel Structure delivers steel structure warehouse solutions for storage, logistics and distribution projects. From design detailing to fabrication and export, we support racking layout, clear height planning, loading access and enclosure system configuration to turn your storage needs into deliverable steel structure buildings.</p>
      <div class="detail-hero-actions">
        <a href="#quote" class="btn btn-primary">Get Project Quotation</a>
        <a href="/en/products/" class="btn btn-outline">View All Products</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Breadcrumb -->
  <nav class="detail-breadcrumb">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/en/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <a href="/en/products/">Products</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span class="current">Steel Warehouse</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- 01 Warehouse Project Requirements -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">01 / Project Requirements</p>
        <h2>What Information Is Needed for a Steel Structure Warehouse</h2>
        <p>The structural configuration of a steel warehouse depends on storage use, racking systems and logistics operations. At the proposal stage, the following information directly influences column grid, clear height, loading area and enclosure system design.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="requirement-grid">
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="req-icon">01</div>
          <h3>Storage Use</h3>
          <p>General storage, logistics distribution, cold storage or special use — different storage methods require different space and enclosure configurations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="req-icon">02</div>
          <h3>Racking System</h3>
          <p>Racking type, dimensions, arrangement and aisle width affect column grid layout and clear height design.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="req-icon">03</div>
          <h3>Clear Height</h3>
          <p>Required storage clear height, racking height and stacking equipment operating space determine eave height and structural configuration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="req-icon">04</div>
          <h3>Loading Access</h3>
          <p>Vehicle type, loading method, dock quantity and turning radius requirements affect building layout and door openings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="req-icon">05</div>
          <h3>Door Requirements</h3>
          <p>Roll-up doors, sectional doors, personnel access quantity and dimensions, and loading dock configuration are determined per operational needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-card reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="req-icon">06</div>
          <h3>Enclosure & Insulation</h3>
          <p>Roof and wall materials, thermal insulation, waterproofing grade and ventilation requirements are determined by storage environment and project requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 Storage & Space Planning -->
  <section class="detail-section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">02 / Storage & Space Planning</p>
        <h2>Space and Column Grid Planning Around Storage Efficiency</h2>
        <p>The core of a steel warehouse is storage efficiency and space utilization. Structural planning needs to accommodate racking layout, goods storage and logistics aisles, rather than simply pursuing maximum span.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="image-text-block">
        <div class="itb-image">
          <img src="/images/products/detail-warehouse-interior.jpg" alt="ZhongSai steel structure warehouse storage space" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="itb-content">
          <h3>Column Grid Coordinated with Racking Layout</h3>
          <p>Column grid spacing is determined based on racking dimensions, aisle width and material handling methods, balancing structural economy with storage space utilization.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Column grid spacing coordinated with racking arrangement and operational aisles</li>
            <li>Clear height accommodates racking storage and stacking equipment operation</li>
            <li>Goods inbound/outbound flow and storage areas reasonably zoned</li>
            <li>Roof and wall systems coordinated with structural frame</li>
            <li>Specific spans, heights and column grids determined per project drawings and requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 Loading & Access Planning -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">03 / Loading & Access</p>
        <h2>Loading Area and Vehicle Access Planning</h2>
        <p>Warehouse loading efficiency directly affects operational cost. Door openings, loading areas and vehicle access need to be planned based on operational methods and vehicle types.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="feature-img" style="background-image: url('/images/container-loading.jpg');"></div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Loading Docks & Door Openings</h3>
            <p>Loading dock quantity, dimensions and height are determined based on vehicle type and operational volume. Door opening dimensions and operating methods are configured per usage requirements.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="feature-img" style="background-image: url('/images/products/detail-loading-dock.jpg');"></div>
          <div class="feature-body">
            <h3>Vehicle Access & Material Flow</h3>
            <p>On-site vehicle access routes, turning radii and loading operational areas are planned based on logistics operational methods. Goods inbound/outbound flow is coordinated with storage areas.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 20px; font-size: 14px; color: #64748b;">* Specific door dimensions, loading dock specifications and turning radius requirements are determined per project operational needs and local codes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 Roof & Wall Envelope -->
  <section class="detail-section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">04 / Roof & Wall Envelope</p>
        <h2>Roof and Wall Cladding Systems</h2>
        <p>The enclosure system of a warehouse directly affects storage environment and operational cost. ZhongSai can supply roof panels, wall panels and supporting cladding materials per project requirements, coordinated with the primary steel structure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="image-text-block reverse">
        <div class="itb-image">
          <img src="/images/products/detail-cladding-system.jpg" alt="Steel warehouse roof and wall cladding systems" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <div class="itb-content">
          <h3>Cladding Configuration Determined Per Storage Environment</h3>
          <p>Roof and wall materials, thermal insulation, waterproofing grade and ventilation configuration are determined based on storage use, local climate and project technical requirements.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Roof and wall panel systems can be supplied together with the primary structure</li>
            <li>Thermal insulation layers configured per storage environment and project requirements</li>
            <li>Roof waterproofing and drainage details designed per project technical requirements</li>
            <li>Natural ventilation and lighting openings arranged per storage needs</li>
          </ul>
          <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <a href="/en/components/roof-wall-cladding-systems/" class="btn btn-outline">View Cladding Systems</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 Fabrication & Export Supply -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">05 / Fabrication & Export</p>
        <h2>Fabrication and Export Supply from Drawings to Delivery</h2>
        <p>ZhongSai operates its own production base, fabricating steel warehouse components per project drawings, covering cutting, assembly, welding, surface treatment and quality control.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-flow">
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="step-num">01</div>
          <h4>Drawings Confirmation</h4>
          <p>Project drawings, BOQ and technical requirements confirmed</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="step-num">02</div>
          <h4>Design Detailing</h4>
          <p>Detailing design and fabrication drawing preparation</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="step-num">03</div>
          <h4>Fabrication</h4>
          <p>Warehouse steel component fabrication organized per drawings</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-4">
          <div class="step-num">04</div>
          <h4>Component Marking</h4>
          <p>Component marking and numbering may be arranged based on shop drawings</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="step-num">05</div>
          <h4>Packing & Loading</h4>
          <p>Packing organized by component type and container loading requirements</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="step-num">06</div>
          <h4>Export Documentation</h4>
          <p>Export documentation support and logistics coordination</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="step-num">07</div>
          <h4>Sea Freight Delivery</h4>
          <p>Container loading and sea freight export arrangement</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step reveal reveal-delay-4">
          <div class="step-num">08</div>
          <h4>Technical Guidance</h4>
          <p>Overseas installation technical guidance (local erection by customer team)</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 28px; display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/en/manufacturing-quality/" class="btn btn-outline">View Manufacturing Capability</a>
        <a href="/en/components/" class="btn btn-outline">View Components & Materials</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GEO Service Boundary -->
  <section class="detail-section dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">Service Boundary</p>
        <h2 style="color: #fff;">What ZhongSai Provides and Does Not Provide</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto;">Clear service scope to avoid project expectation gaps.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="geo-boundary">
        <div class="geo-box include">
          <h4>ZhongSai Provides</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Design detailing and fabrication drawing support</li>
            <li>Steel warehouse component fabrication</li>
            <li>Steel beams, columns, purlins and component supply</li>
            <li>Roof and wall cladding system coordination</li>
            <li>Component marking, packing and container loading</li>
            <li>Export documentation support and logistics coordination</li>
            <li>Overseas installation technical guidance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="geo-box exclude">
          <h4>ZhongSai Does Not Directly Undertake</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Local construction in the project country</li>
            <li>Local foundation construction</li>
            <li>Local general contracting / EPC</li>
            <li>Local finishing and MEP works</li>
            <li>Customs brokerage as a licensed customs broker</li>
            <li>Freight forwarding as a licensed freight forwarder</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 06 What We Need for Quotation -->
  <section class="detail-section alt" id="quote-info">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">06 / Quotation Information</p>
        <h2>What Information Is Needed for a Warehouse Quotation</h2>
        <p>The more complete the project information, the more accurate the quotation. Storage use, racking layout and loading requirements directly influence structural configuration and pricing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-info-grid">
        <div class="quote-info-card drawing">
          <h4>Have Drawings / BOQ</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Project country</li>
            <li>Architectural / structural drawings</li>
            <li>Bill of Quantities (BOQ)</li>
            <li>Project technical specifications</li>
            <li>Racking / loading special requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="quote-info-card no-drawing">
          <h4>No Complete Drawings Yet</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Project country</li>
            <li>Warehouse use (general storage / logistics / cold storage)</li>
            <li>Length / width / height (reference dimensions)</li>
            <li>Racking type and clear height requirements</li>
            <li>Loading method and door requirements</li>
            <li>Insulation / ventilation special requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="quote-note">* Initial proposal and quotation require needs assessment based on project use and basic parameters. Final proposal and pricing are subject to drawing and technical requirement confirmation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 07 FAQ -->
  <section class="detail-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center;">07 / FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Steel Warehouses</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-faq">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>What information is needed for a steel warehouse quotation?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              You need to provide project country, warehouse use, reference dimensions (length, width, height), racking type and clear height requirements, loading method and door requirements, and insulation/ventilation special requirements. Complete drawings and BOQ enable more accurate pricing.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can the warehouse be planned around racking and clear-height requirements?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. ZhongSai can plan the warehouse layout based on racking type, dimensions, arrangement and required clear height, combined with column grid layout and structural economy. Specific configuration requires project drawings and local design requirements.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Can roof and wall cladding systems be supplied with the steel structure?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <div class="faq-answer-inner">
              Yes. ZhongSai can supply roof panels, wall panels, insulation layers and supporting cladding materials together with the primary steel structure, coordinated in design and supply. Specific cladding configuration is determined per project technical requirements.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 08 Quote CTA + QuoteForm -->
  <section class="detail-section dark" id="quote">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading reveal" style="text-align: center;">
        <p class="section-index" style="justify-content: center; color: #f59e0b;">08 / Get Quotation</p>
        <h2 style="color: #fff;">Submit Your Steel Warehouse Project Requirements</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);">Upload drawings if available, or submit basic project requirements if you don't have complete drawings yet.</p>
      </div>
      <QuoteForm lang="en" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // FAQ toggle
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const item = btn.closest('.faq-item');
      const isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');
      item.classList.toggle('open');
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', !isOpen);
    });
  });

  // Scroll reveal
  const revealElements = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach(entry => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.style.opacity = '1';
          entry.target.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });
    revealElements.forEach(el => {
      el.style.opacity = '0';
      el.style.transform = 'translateY(24px)';
      el.style.transition = 'opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease';
      observer.observe(el);
    });
  }
</script>
